@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-nouns`
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-rules`
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-reading`

-- ca-tests-reading.l4
--
-- The rules for reading an enactment that pass 2 adds: sections 3(2), 3(3), 4, 5(1), 8(3), 8.1, 8.3, 10, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16, 18(1) and (2),
-- 21(2), 25(2), 33, 36, 38, 40, 41(2) to (5), 42 and 45.
-- Expected values are written from the text of the Act, before the module was run.
-- TRUE where the text states the condition and it is met; FALSE only where the text says "shall not be deemed" or a subsection says a thing
-- is not so; `#ASSERT REFUSED` for a case the text does not address.

§ `Section 3(2): the Act applies to its own interpretation`

-- "The provisions of this Act apply to the interpretation of this Act."  (FORK F-3-2: no contrary-intention qualifier is read in.)
#ASSERT `a provision of the Act applies to the interpretation of the Act`

§ `Section 3(3): a rule of construction that the Act does not exclude`

-- "Nothing in this Act excludes the application to an enactment of a rule of construction applicable to that enactment and not inconsistent
-- with this Act."
#ASSERT `the Act does not exclude the application to an enactment of a rule of construction which` TRUE `and` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the Act does not exclude the application to an enactment of a rule of construction which` TRUE `and` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the Act does not exclude the application to an enactment of a rule of construction which` FALSE `and` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the Act does not exclude the application to an enactment of a rule of construction which` FALSE `and` FALSE)

§ `Section 4: the enacting clause of an Act`

-- (1) "The enacting clause of an Act may be in the following form: ‘Her Majesty, by and with the advice and consent of the Senate and House
-- of Commons of Canada, enacts as follows:’."
#ASSERT `the enacting clause of an Act may be in the form` "Her Majesty, by and with the advice and consent of the Senate and House of Commons of Canada, enacts as follows:"
-- "may be": another form is not said to be forbidden.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the enacting clause of an Act may be in the form` "The King, by and with the advice and consent of the Senate and House of Commons of Canada, enacts as follows:")
-- (2) The enacting clause follows the preamble, if any, and the provisions of the body follow it in a concise and enunciative form.
#ASSERT `an Act is arranged as section 4(2) requires where` TRUE `and the enacting clause follows it` TRUE `and the provisions follow the clause` TRUE `and are concise and enunciative` TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act is arranged as section 4(2) requires where` FALSE `and the enacting clause follows it` FALSE `and the provisions follow the clause` TRUE `and are concise and enunciative` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`an Act is arranged as section 4(2) requires where` TRUE `and the enacting clause follows it` FALSE `and the provisions follow the clause` TRUE `and are concise and enunciative` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`an Act is arranged as section 4(2) requires where` TRUE `and the enacting clause follows it` TRUE `and the provisions follow the clause` FALSE `and are concise and enunciative` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`an Act is arranged as section 4(2) requires where` TRUE `and the enacting clause follows it` TRUE `and the provisions follow the clause` TRUE `and are concise and enunciative` FALSE)

§ `Section 5(1): the endorsement of the day of assent`

-- "The Clerk of the Parliaments shall endorse on every Act, immediately after its title, the day, month and year when the Act was assented
-- to in Her Majesty’s name and the endorsement shall be a part of the Act."
#ASSERT (`the endorsement the Clerk of the Parliaments shall make on an Act assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 10))'s `where it is placed` EQUALS "immediately after the title of the Act"
#ASSERT (`the endorsement the Clerk of the Parliaments shall make on an Act assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 10))'s `the day it records` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
#ASSERT (`the endorsement the Clerk of the Parliaments shall make on an Act assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 10))'s `it is a part of the Act`

§ `Section 8(3): an old Act with extra-territorial operation`

-- "Every Act now in force enacted prior to December 11, 1931 that expressly or by necessary or reasonable implication was intended ... to
-- have extra-territorial operation shall be construed as if, at the date of its enactment, the Parliament of Canada had full power ..."
#ASSERT `an Act is construed as if Parliament had full power to make laws having extra-territorial operation where` TRUE `and was enacted on` (YMD 1931 12 10) `and` TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act is construed as if Parliament had full power to make laws having extra-territorial operation where` TRUE `and was enacted on` (YMD 1900 1 1) `and` TRUE
-- December 11, 1931 itself is not "prior to" December 11, 1931.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`an Act is construed as if Parliament had full power to make laws having extra-territorial operation where` TRUE `and was enacted on` (YMD 1931 12 11) `and` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`an Act is construed as if Parliament had full power to make laws having extra-territorial operation where` TRUE `and was enacted on` (YMD 1932 1 1) `and` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`an Act is construed as if Parliament had full power to make laws having extra-territorial operation where` FALSE `and was enacted on` (YMD 1931 12 10) `and` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`an Act is construed as if Parliament had full power to make laws having extra-territorial operation where` TRUE `and was enacted on` (YMD 1931 12 10) `and` FALSE)

§ `Section 8.1: the common law and the civil law`

-- "Both the common law and the civil law are equally authoritative and recognized sources of the law of property and civil rights in Canada."
#ASSERT `is an equally authoritative and recognized source of the law of property and civil rights in Canada` `the common law`
#ASSERT `is an equally authoritative and recognized source of the law of property and civil rights in Canada` `the civil law`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`is an equally authoritative and recognized source of the law of property and civil rights in Canada` `a source of neither kind`)
-- "unless otherwise provided by law, ... reference must be made to the rules, principles and concepts in force in the province at the time the
-- enactment is being applied."
#ASSERT `the province's rules, principles and concepts to which reference is made, unless` FALSE EQUALS `those in force in the province at the time the enactment is being applied`
#ASSERT NOT (`the province's rules, principles and concepts to which reference is made, unless` FALSE EQUALS `those in force at some other time`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the province's rules, principles and concepts to which reference is made, unless` TRUE)

§ `Section 8.3: the rights of Indigenous peoples`

-- "Every enactment is to be construed as upholding the Aboriginal and treaty rights of Indigenous peoples recognized and affirmed by section 35
-- of the Constitution Act, 1982, and not as abrogating or derogating from them."
#ASSERT `a construction of an enactment is permitted as to a right where` TRUE `and` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a construction of an enactment is permitted as to a right where` TRUE `and` TRUE)
-- The section speaks of those rights and no other.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a construction of an enactment is permitted as to a right where` FALSE `and` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a construction of an enactment is permitted as to a right where` FALSE `and` FALSE)
-- (2) "Indigenous peoples has the meaning assigned by the definition aboriginal peoples of Canada in subsection 35(2) of the Constitution Act, 1982."
#ASSERT `a people are Indigenous peoples for section 8.3(1) where` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a people are Indigenous peoples for section 8.3(1) where` FALSE)
-- Section 3(1) applies "every provision" of the Act "unless a contrary intention appears", so it lets a contrary intention displace this
-- provision as any other (convention C-3-1-GATE): the gate answers it, and the function above takes it as asked once the gate says yes.
#ASSERT `a provision of the Act applies to an enactment unless` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a provision of the Act applies to an enactment unless` TRUE)

§ `Section 10: the law is always speaking`

-- "The law shall be considered as always speaking, and where a matter or thing is expressed in the present tense, it shall be applied to the
-- circumstances as they arise."
#ASSERT `the law is considered as always speaking`
#ASSERT `the circumstances to which a matter or thing is applied, if it is expressed in` `the present tense` EQUALS `the circumstances as they arise`
#ASSERT NOT (`the circumstances to which a matter or thing is applied, if it is expressed in` `the present tense` EQUALS `the circumstances as they stood when it was enacted`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the circumstances to which a matter or thing is applied, if it is expressed in` `some other tense`)

§ `Section 12: enactments are remedial`

-- "Every enactment is deemed remedial, and shall be given such fair, large and liberal construction and interpretation as best ensures the
-- attainment of its objects."
#ASSERT `an enactment is deemed remedial`
#ASSERT `a construction is the one section 12 gives where` TRUE `and` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a construction is the one section 12 gives where` TRUE `and` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a construction is the one section 12 gives where` FALSE `and` TRUE)

§ `Section 13: the preamble`

-- "The preamble of an enactment shall be read as a part of the enactment intended to assist in explaining its purport and object."
#ASSERT `the standing section 13 gives to` `the preamble` EQUALS `a part of the enactment, intended to assist in explaining its purport and object`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the standing section 13 gives to` `a marginal note`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the standing section 13 gives to` `another part of the printed text`)

§ `Section 14: marginal notes and historical references`

-- "Marginal notes and references to former enactments that appear after the end of a section or other division in an enactment form no part
-- of the enactment, but are inserted for convenience of reference only."  (FORK F-14-SCOPE.)
#ASSERT `the standing section 14 gives to` `a marginal note` EQUALS `no part of the enactment, inserted for convenience of reference only`
#ASSERT `the standing section 14 gives to` `a reference to a former enactment that appears after the end of a section or other division` EQUALS `no part of the enactment, inserted for convenience of reference only`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the standing section 14 gives to` `a reference to a former enactment that appears elsewhere in the printed text`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the standing section 14 gives to` `the preamble`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the standing section 14 gives to` `another part of the printed text`)

§ `Section 15: definitions and interpretation provisions in an enactment`

-- (1) and (2)(a): applies to every provision of the enactment, including those that contain it, only if a contrary intention does not appear.
#ASSERT `a definition or rule of interpretation in an enactment applies to a provision of the same enactment, including the provision that contains it, unless` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a definition or rule of interpretation in an enactment applies to a provision of the same enactment, including the provision that contains it, unless` TRUE)
-- (2)(b): applicable to all other enactments relating to the same subject-matter unless a contrary intention appears.
#ASSERT `an interpretation provision of an enactment applies to another enactment where` TRUE `unless` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`an interpretation provision of an enactment applies to another enactment where` TRUE `unless` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`an interpretation provision of an enactment applies to another enactment where` FALSE `unless` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`an interpretation provision of an enactment applies to another enactment where` FALSE `unless` TRUE)

§ `Section 16: words in regulations`

-- "Where an enactment confers power to make regulations, expressions used in the regulations have the same respective meanings as in the
-- enactment conferring the power."
#ASSERT `the meaning of an expression used in regulations made under an enactment which` TRUE `gives the expression the meaning` "a place where goods are kept for sale" EQUALS "a place where goods are kept for sale"
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the meaning of an expression used in regulations made under an enactment which` FALSE `gives the expression the meaning` "a place where goods are kept for sale")

§ `Section 18(1) and (2): proclamations`

-- (1) "Where an enactment authorizes the issue of a proclamation, the proclamation shall be understood to be a proclamation of the Governor in Council."
#ASSERT `a proclamation is understood to be a proclamation of whom, where` TRUE EQUALS "the Governor in Council"
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a proclamation is understood to be a proclamation of whom, where` FALSE)
-- (2) "Where the Governor General is authorized to issue a proclamation, the proclamation shall be understood to be a proclamation issued under an
-- order of the Governor in Council, but it is not necessary to mention in the proclamation that it is issued under such an order."
#ASSERT `a proclamation is understood to be issued under an order of the Governor in Council, where` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a proclamation is understood to be issued under an order of the Governor in Council, where` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`it is necessary to mention in the proclamation that it is issued under an order, where` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`it is necessary to mention in the proclamation that it is issued under an order, where` FALSE)

§ `Section 21(2): the name of a corporation with an English and a French form`

-- "Where an enactment establishes a corporation and in each of the English and French versions of the enactment the name of the corporation is
-- in the form only of the language of that version, the name of the corporation shall consist of the form of its name in each of the versions."
#ASSERT `the name of a corporation an enactment establishes, with` "Canadian Widgets Corporation" `in the English version and` "Société canadienne des gadgets" `in the French version, where` TRUE EQUALS LIST "Canadian Widgets Corporation", "Société canadienne des gadgets"
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the name of a corporation an enactment establishes, with` "Canadian Widgets Corporation" `in the English version and` "Société canadienne des gadgets" `in the French version, where` FALSE)

§ `Section 25(2): copies printed by the Queen's Printer`

-- "Every copy of an enactment having printed thereon what purports to be the name or title of the Queen’s Printer and Controller of Stationery
-- or the Queen’s Printer is deemed to be a copy purporting to be printed by the Queen’s Printer for Canada."
#ASSERT `a copy of an enactment is deemed to be a copy purporting to be printed by the Queen's Printer for Canada, when it has printed on it` "the Queen’s Printer and Controller of Stationery"
#ASSERT `a copy of an enactment is deemed to be a copy purporting to be printed by the Queen's Printer for Canada, when it has printed on it` "the Queen’s Printer"
-- FORK F-QUEENS: taken, the titles styled for the reigning Sovereign count.
#ASSERT `a copy of an enactment is deemed to be a copy purporting to be printed by the Queen's Printer for Canada, when it has printed on it` "the King’s Printer and Controller of Stationery"
#ASSERT `a copy of an enactment is deemed to be a copy purporting to be printed by the Queen's Printer for Canada, when it has printed on it` "the King’s Printer"
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a copy of an enactment is deemed to be a copy purporting to be printed by the Queen's Printer for Canada, when it has printed on it` "the Printer")

§ `Section 33: gender, number and grammatical forms`

-- (1) "Words importing female persons include male persons and corporations and words importing male persons include female persons and corporations."
#ASSERT `words importing` `female persons` `include those importing` `male persons`
#ASSERT `words importing` `female persons` `include those importing` `corporations`
#ASSERT `words importing` `male persons` `include those importing` `female persons`
#ASSERT `words importing` `male persons` `include those importing` `corporations`
#ASSERT `words importing` `female persons` `include those importing` `female persons`
#ASSERT `words importing` `male persons` `include those importing` `male persons`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`words importing` `female persons` `include those importing` `something else`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`words importing` `male persons` `include those importing` `something else`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`words importing` `corporations` `include those importing` `male persons`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`words importing` `something else` `include those importing` `female persons`)
-- (2) "Words in the singular include the plural, and words in the plural include the singular."
#ASSERT `words in` `the singular` `include words in` `the plural`
#ASSERT `words in` `the plural` `include words in` `the singular`
-- (3) "Where a word is defined, other parts of speech and grammatical forms of the same word have corresponding meanings."
#ASSERT `a form of a defined word has a corresponding meaning` `another part of speech of the word defined`
#ASSERT `a form of a defined word has a corresponding meaning` `another grammatical form of the word defined`
#ASSERT `a form of a defined word has a corresponding meaning` `the word as defined`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a form of a defined word has a corresponding meaning` `a different word`)

§ `Section 36: telegraph`

-- "The expression telegraph and its derivatives, in an enactment or in an Act of the legislature of any province enacted before that province
-- became part of Canada on any subject that is within the legislative powers of Parliament, are deemed not to include the word ‘telephone’
-- or its derivatives."
#ASSERT NOT (`the expression telegraph includes the word telephone, used` `in an enactment`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the expression telegraph includes the word telephone, used` `in an Act of a provincial legislature enacted before the province became part of Canada, on a subject within the legislative powers of Parliament`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the expression telegraph includes the word telephone, used` `in an Act of a provincial legislature enacted before the province became part of Canada, on a subject not within the legislative powers of Parliament`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the expression telegraph includes the word telephone, used` `somewhere else`)

§ `Section 38: common names`

-- "The name commonly applied to any country, place, body, ... means the ... to which the name is commonly applied, although the name is not the
-- formal or extended designation thereof."
#ASSERT `the name means the thing to which it is commonly applied where` TRUE `whether or not` TRUE
#ASSERT `the name means the thing to which it is commonly applied where` TRUE `whether or not` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the name means the thing to which it is commonly applied where` FALSE `whether or not` TRUE)

§ `Section 40: citation of an enactment`

-- (1)(a) An Act may be cited by chapter number in the Revised Statutes, by chapter number in the volume of Acts, or by long title or short title.
#ASSERT `it is permitted to cite` `an Act of Parliament` `in the way` `by its chapter number in the Revised Statutes`
#ASSERT `it is permitted to cite` `an Act of Parliament` `in the way` `by its chapter number in the volume of Acts for the year or regnal year in which it was enacted`
#ASSERT `it is permitted to cite` `an Act of Parliament` `in the way` `by its long title`
#ASSERT `it is permitted to cite` `an Act of Parliament` `in the way` `by its short title`
-- (1)(b) A regulation may be cited by long title or short title, by the Act under which it was made, or by the number or designation under
-- which the Clerk of the Privy Council registered it.
#ASSERT `it is permitted to cite` `a regulation` `in the way` `by its long title`
#ASSERT `it is permitted to cite` `a regulation` `in the way` `by its short title`
#ASSERT `it is permitted to cite` `a regulation` `in the way` `by the Act under which it was made`
#ASSERT `it is permitted to cite` `a regulation` `in the way` `by the number or designation under which it was registered by the Clerk of the Privy Council`
-- "may be cited": a way the text does not list is not said to be forbidden.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`it is permitted to cite` `an Act of Parliament` `in the way` `by the Act under which it was made`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`it is permitted to cite` `a regulation` `in the way` `by its chapter number in the Revised Statutes`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`it is permitted to cite` `an Act of Parliament` `in the way` `by some other description`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`it is permitted to cite` `an Act of a legislature` `in the way` `by its short title`)
-- (2) "A citation of or reference to an enactment is deemed to be a citation of or reference to the enactment as amended."  (FORK F-40-2-DATE:
-- taken, as amended up to the day on which the citation is read and applied.)
#ASSERT `the amendments a citation of an enactment includes, read and applied on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `when the enactment was amended on` (LIST (YMD 2025 1 1), (YMD 2026 6 1), (YMD 2026 6 2)) EQUALS LIST (YMD 2025 1 1), (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT `the amendments a citation of an enactment includes, read and applied on` (YMD 2024 12 31) `when the enactment was amended on` (LIST (YMD 2025 1 1), (YMD 2026 6 1)) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the amendments a citation of an enactment includes, read and applied on` (YMD 2030 1 1) `when the enactment was amended on` (LIST (YMD 2025 1 1), (YMD 2026 6 1)) EQUALS LIST (YMD 2025 1 1), (YMD 2026 6 1)

§ `Section 41(2): where a reference in an enactment points`

-- (2) A reference to a part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form is a reference to one of the enactment in which it occurs.
#ASSERT `the place a reference in an enactment points to, when it is a reference to` `a part` EQUALS "a part of the enactment in which the reference occurs"
#ASSERT `the place a reference in an enactment points to, when it is a reference to` `a division` EQUALS "a division of the enactment in which the reference occurs"
#ASSERT `the place a reference in an enactment points to, when it is a reference to` `a section` EQUALS "a section of the enactment in which the reference occurs"
#ASSERT `the place a reference in an enactment points to, when it is a reference to` `a schedule` EQUALS "a schedule of the enactment in which the reference occurs"
#ASSERT `the place a reference in an enactment points to, when it is a reference to` `an appendix` EQUALS "an appendix of the enactment in which the reference occurs"
#ASSERT `the place a reference in an enactment points to, when it is a reference to` `a form` EQUALS "a form of the enactment in which the reference occurs"
-- (3) A reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, clause or subclause is a reference to one of the section, subsection, paragraph,
-- subparagraph or clause, as the case may be, in which it occurs.
#ASSERT `the place a reference in an enactment points to, when it is a reference to` `a subsection` EQUALS "a subsection of the section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause, as the case may be, in which the reference occurs"
#ASSERT `the place a reference in an enactment points to, when it is a reference to` `a paragraph` EQUALS "a paragraph of the section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause, as the case may be, in which the reference occurs"
#ASSERT `the place a reference in an enactment points to, when it is a reference to` `a subparagraph` EQUALS "a subparagraph of the section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause, as the case may be, in which the reference occurs"
#ASSERT `the place a reference in an enactment points to, when it is a reference to` `a clause` EQUALS "a clause of the section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause, as the case may be, in which the reference occurs"
#ASSERT `the place a reference in an enactment points to, when it is a reference to` `a subclause` EQUALS "a subclause of the section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause, as the case may be, in which the reference occurs"
-- (4) A reference to regulations is a reference to regulations made under the enactment in which it occurs.
#ASSERT `the place a reference in an enactment points to, when it is a reference to` `regulations` EQUALS "regulations made under the enactment in which the reference occurs"
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the place a reference in an enactment points to, when it is a reference to` `anything else`)
-- (5) A reference by number or letter to a division or line of another enactment is a reference to it as printed by authority of law.
#ASSERT `a reference to another enactment is read as a reference to the provision` TRUE EQUALS "the section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, clause, subclause or other division or line of such other enactment as printed by authority of law"
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a reference to another enactment is read as a reference to the provision` FALSE)

§ `Section 42: repeal and amendment of an Act`

-- (1) "Every Act shall be so construed as to reserve to Parliament the power of repealing or amending it, and of revoking, restricting or
-- modifying any power, privilege or advantage thereby vested in or granted to any person."
#ASSERT `Parliament has reserved to itself the power to` `repeal the Act`
#ASSERT `Parliament has reserved to itself the power to` `amend the Act`
#ASSERT `Parliament has reserved to itself the power to` `revoke a power, privilege or advantage that the Act vests in or grants to a person`
#ASSERT `Parliament has reserved to itself the power to` `restrict a power, privilege or advantage that the Act vests in or grants to a person`
#ASSERT `Parliament has reserved to itself the power to` `modify a power, privilege or advantage that the Act vests in or grants to a person`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`Parliament has reserved to itself the power to` `some other thing`)
-- (2) "An Act may be amended or repealed by an Act passed in the same session of Parliament."
#ASSERT `an Act may be amended or repealed by an Act passed in the same session where` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`an Act may be amended or repealed by an Act passed in the same session where` FALSE)
-- (3) "An amending enactment, as far as consistent with the tenor thereof, shall be construed as part of the enactment that it amends."
#ASSERT `an amending enactment is construed as part of the enactment that it amends, so far as` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`an amending enactment is construed as part of the enactment that it amends, so far as` FALSE)

§ `Section 45: what a repeal, an amendment or a re-enactment does not imply`

-- (1) Repeal is not deemed to be or involve a declaration that the enactment was previously in force.
#ASSERT NOT (`it is deemed to be or to involve` `a declaration that the enactment was previously in force` `when the enactment is subject to` `repealing it in whole`)
#ASSERT NOT (`it is deemed to be or to involve` `a declaration that the enactment was previously in force` `when the enactment is subject to` `repealing it in part`)
-- (2) Amendment is not deemed to be or involve a declaration that the law under the enactment was different from the law as amended.
#ASSERT NOT (`it is deemed to be or to involve` `a declaration that the law under the enactment was different from the law as amended` `when the enactment is subject to` `amending it`)
-- (3) Repeal or amendment is not deemed to involve any declaration as to the previous state of the law.
#ASSERT NOT (`it is deemed to be or to involve` `a declaration as to the previous state of the law` `when the enactment is subject to` `repealing it in whole`)
#ASSERT NOT (`it is deemed to be or to involve` `a declaration as to the previous state of the law` `when the enactment is subject to` `repealing it in part`)
#ASSERT NOT (`it is deemed to be or to involve` `a declaration as to the previous state of the law` `when the enactment is subject to` `amending it`)
-- Subsection (3) says "any declaration", so it reaches the declarations of (1) and (2) as well.
#ASSERT NOT (`it is deemed to be or to involve` `a declaration that the law under the enactment was different from the law as amended` `when the enactment is subject to` `repealing it in whole`)
#ASSERT NOT (`it is deemed to be or to involve` `a declaration that the enactment was previously in force` `when the enactment is subject to` `amending it`)
-- (4) A re-enactment, revision, consolidation or amendment is not deemed to be or involve an adoption of the construction placed on the language.
#ASSERT NOT (`it is deemed to be or to involve` `an adoption of the construction placed on the language used, or on similar language, by judicial decision or otherwise` `when the enactment is subject to` `re-enacting it`)
#ASSERT NOT (`it is deemed to be or to involve` `an adoption of the construction placed on the language used, or on similar language, by judicial decision or otherwise` `when the enactment is subject to` `revising it`)
#ASSERT NOT (`it is deemed to be or to involve` `an adoption of the construction placed on the language used, or on similar language, by judicial decision or otherwise` `when the enactment is subject to` `consolidating it`)
#ASSERT NOT (`it is deemed to be or to involve` `an adoption of the construction placed on the language used, or on similar language, by judicial decision or otherwise` `when the enactment is subject to` `amending it`)
-- A repeal and the adoption of a construction: not addressed.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`it is deemed to be or to involve` `an adoption of the construction placed on the language used, or on similar language, by judicial decision or otherwise` `when the enactment is subject to` `repealing it in whole`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`it is deemed to be or to involve` `an adoption of the construction placed on the language used, or on similar language, by judicial decision or otherwise` `when the enactment is subject to` `repealing it in part`)
-- A re-enactment, revision or consolidation and the other three: not addressed.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`it is deemed to be or to involve` `a declaration that the enactment was previously in force` `when the enactment is subject to` `re-enacting it`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`it is deemed to be or to involve` `a declaration as to the previous state of the law` `when the enactment is subject to` `revising it`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`it is deemed to be or to involve` `a declaration that the law under the enactment was different from the law as amended` `when the enactment is subject to` `consolidating it`)
-- Anything else done to an enactment: not addressed.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`it is deemed to be or to involve` `a declaration that the enactment was previously in force` `when the enactment is subject to` `something else`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`it is deemed to be or to involve` `an adoption of the construction placed on the language used, or on similar language, by judicial decision or otherwise` `when the enactment is subject to` `something else`)
